This is Kilimo AI, a WhatsApp-first agronomy bot for Kenyan smallholder farmers.

Stack: Next.js 15 App Router, TypeScript, Tailwind 4, Supabase (Postgres + pgvector), Anthropic Claude, Voyage AI embeddings, Twilio WhatsApp.

Rules:
1. Never use em dashes anywhere. Use commas, colons, semicolons, or restructured sentences.
2. Server-only code (Supabase service role, Anthropic key, Voyage key, Twilio secrets) must never leak into client bundles. Use "server-only" import guard.
3. Every LLM response is validated with Zod before use. Malformed responses log and fall back gracefully.
4. Phone numbers are always SHA-256 hashed with PHONE_HASH_SALT before logging.
5. Twilio webhook signature must be verified on every request.
6. Prompt versioning: any change to the system prompt bumps the version string in src/lib/prompt.ts and is recorded in eval_runs.
7. Every new KB entry must include both English and Swahili question and answer, plus a real citation.
8. Never invent scientific dosages, disease names, or agronomy facts. When unsure, mark TODO and flag for agronomist review.
9. Prefer server components. Use client components only when interactivity requires it.
10. Follow the design system in PROMPT.md section 9. Do not introduce new colors.
